From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:08:27 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] lynx-rotation

Some Lynx carts are made to be held turned left or right. The picture
stays the Lynx LCD as drawn and the player turns the handheld; for a
right-turned cart slot sets lynx_rot_screen to 180, the core turns the
pad half a turn and asks for SET_ROTATION 2, and slot answers it by
drawing the frame upside down and mirrored (a reversed copy into the
same centred box), so every turned cart is held the same way. Upright
and left carts keep 0, the raw picture and pad. Quarter turns are
refused. The Lynx Screen section gains Flip Right Carts (On by default,
Config/lynx_flip.txt); Off draws right carts as made.

Which way a cart is turned: Config/lynx_rotation.txt (<stem> = left,
right or none) wins, then a list by title for dumps whose header says
nothing (Klax and Gauntlet: The Third Encounter right, Lexis and NFL
Football left, matched on the stem or the header title), then the LNX
header byte at 0x3a. L and R reach the game as Option 1 and 2; SELECT
stays slot's.

The list by title and the override file follow nelynes/slotPlus d7d0e74
and the held-turned play 185257a (GPL-3.0),
https://github.com/nelynes/slotPlus/commit/d7d0e74
https://github.com/nelynes/slotPlus/commit/185257a
